--
N5008 [over.match.funcs.general]/4-5, [over.ics.rank]/3.2.6: for `d.load(0)'
on a non-const `derived', the implicit object parameters are `const base &'
and `const volatile base &'; both bindings are reference bindings of the
same derived-to-base kind, and the one to the less cv-qualified type is
better, so the const overload is selected.  The front end reports
"symbol 'load' does not uniquely resolve" when the call goes through a
BASE class (a direct `b.load(0)' on base is fine).  This is libstdc++'s
std::atomic<unsigned> (__atomic_base::load() const and load() const
volatile) used by __atomic_futex_unsigned::_M_load / _M_load_and_test
(atomic_futex.h:84/155, <future>, cpp11_future_header in the round-163
audit).  Header-free.  Pre-existing (round-162 snapshot bin51 fails the
same way).
